o underwent several revisions and  there were some fascinating early  versions as well as this much darker  version of Haller and her costume her  headdress was also going to be  weaponized in an interview with Vanity  Fair VFX supervisor Jake Morrison  mentioned that an early design of  Hallows headgear included antlers that  could turn into face masks shields  almost like samurai style outfits I'm  guessing these might have been scrapped  because when producers have got  expensive famous actors for a big movie  they don't necessarily want them to  spend a lot of screen time with their  faces covered up while we didn't get  those extra features on Hellas costume  we still saw her in some pretty  fantastic action scenes that show off  her incredible power and the amazing  scene where Heller takes out the entire  elite Asgardian army single-handedly is  an extraordinary demonstration of her  capabilities but there are actually  multiple versions of this scene  originally it was meant to be even  longer but was cut back to avoid  repetition and extending production days  on top of that Jake Morrison explained  that it was actually filmed as a single  continuous action shot in which a  revolving camera tracked Heller as she  plowed through and killed everybody I  think a single camera  broken take of that scene could have  been amazing to watch however I can  imagine it would have been really  difficult to get just right and even  tiny errors in the Strunk choreography  or timing could have spoiled it  Martha has said that the scene was late  and re-edited to make it more percussive  which sounds like it perhaps wasn't  quite up to scratch to work as a single  shot and we also almost got a scene  between Heller and the destroyer the  Asgardian automate him from the first  Thor movie in the original draft when  Heller is looking for Heimdall sword so  she can operate the Bifrost bridge she  goes to look inside the weapons vault as  she enters the destroyer is activated 